## 3. Write jQuery to show the use of click(), hover(), on(), trigger(), off() events.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Basic jQuery</title>

    <script src="jquery-3.6.1.min.js"></script>

    <script>
        $(document).ready(function () {

            $("#b1").hover(
                function () {
                    $(this).css("background", "lightblue");
                },
                function () {
                    $(this).css("background", "");
                }
            );

            $("p").on("click", function () {
                $(this).css("background", "yellow");
            });

            $("#b2").click(function () {
                $("p").off("click");
            });

            $("#b3").on("click", function () {
                $("#t1").hide();
            });

            $("input").on("select", function () {
                $(this).after("<span> Text Marked!</span>");
            });

            $("#b4").click(function () {
                $("input").trigger("select");
            });

        });
    </script>
</head>

<body>

    <button id="b1">Hover</button>
    <br><br>

    <p>Welcome to Mulund College</p>
    <br>

    <p>Romal: 239720</p>
    <br>

    <button id="b2">Off</button>
    <br><br>

    <p id="t1">Hello Romal</p>

    <button id="b3">On</button>
    <br><br>

    <input type="text" value="Romal 239720">
    <br><br>

    <button id="b4">Trigger</button>

</body>
</html>
```

OUTPUT:
Hover over the Hover button → background changes.
Click a paragraph → background changes to yellow.
Click Off → paragraph click events are removed.
Click On → "Hello Romal" is hidden.
Select text inside input → "Text Marked!" appears.
Click Trigger → select event is triggered.

## 4. Write a jQuery to create animated show and hide effect.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Basic jQuery</title>

    <script src="jquery-3.6.1.min.js"></script>

    <script>
        $(document).ready(function () {

            $("#b1").click(function () {
                $("p").hide(1000);
            });

